# Only honoured when presets are APPLIED: first boot of a fresh `bootc
# install` (enable-only mode) or an admin running `systemctl preset-all`
# (full mode). A rebase re-runs neither -- the /etc wants symlinks written at
# image build (see the Containerfile's finalize step) are what actually
# enable these units on a rebased system.
#
# Every unit the finalize step enables must ALSO be listed here. Presets are
# policy, not symlinks, so this file cannot recreate the two-symlink problem
# the Containerfile warns about -- but greenboot ships no preset entry of its
# own, so a `systemctl preset-all` run in full mode would fall through to
# Fedora's `disable *` and quietly disarm automatic rollback. The
# Containerfile asserts this list and its enablements agree.
enable scx.service
enable greenboot-healthcheck.service
enable pulsar-flatpaks.service
disable NetworkManager-wait-online.service
